      "mention": "Vardan Mamikonean",
      "label": "person",
      "paragraph_id": "p003",
      "context": "On 2nd June 451 AD an Armenian rebellion was crushed by Sasanian forces at Awarayr near the region’s south-east border, decisively ending an uprising primarily comprised of Christian nobles that had begun the year prior in response to attempts by Yazdgerd II (r. AD 438–57) to convert the Armenian nobility to Zoroastrianism. The battle resulted in the death of rebel leader Vardan Mamikonean and many of his allies, who were canonised by the Armenian Church and became exemplars for resistance against foreign oppression. However, the following paper concerns itself not with these saints, but with survivors imprisoned after the rebellion.",
